rgin Islands?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The United States purchased the islands from Denmark in 1917; before the sale, they were known as the Danish West Indies.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7ac1-a1a9-08a0d90eaf9b","description":"Denmark","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-749b-8bcc-1b894860787f","description":"Norway","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7618-a3ab-f8d75688bb39","description":"Sweden","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-779f-8be6-7f835308c7ec","description":"Finland","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-741f-bc07-aab641c24dcd","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which nursery rhyme did Thomas Edison recite in his first recording on the phonograph in 1877?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Edison recited \'Mary Had a Little Lamb\' to test his tinfoil phonograph in 1877.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7b4f-b27f-d33704b8c4de","description":"Mary Had A Little Lamb","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7611-b8ed-747f6643b7fa","description":"Twinkle Twinkle Little Star","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7688-803b-7b0cdf996ea4","description":"Humpty Dumpty","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7386-9e18-e3c392cb0bbd","description":"Three Blind Mice","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f79-966b-ca150e4e15d6","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the 10th president of the USA, in term during the period 1841\u20131845?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"John Tyler was the first vice president to assume the presidency after a president died in office, establishing that the successor would serve as president rather than acting president.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7825-b715-9fe5fe4c3b5f","description":"John Tyler","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-74fe-b5c0-c433a594087d","description":"Lyndon Johnson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-74d6-bf9d-84a28d27c691","description":"James Buchana