 of Scotland; he became James I of England when he inherited the English crown.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-747a-a5c5-0ee43ac8cb03","description":"Mary Queen Of Scots","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-78de-a7cb-2e02c43f82dc","description":"Elizabeth I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7eb0-b7e5-5ff3d49affe1","description":"Victoria","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-78b9-a9d0-8f1fd09ef3d1","description":"Jane Seymour","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-748b-a48a-70f0129da805","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the last of the Apache warrior chiefs?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Geronimo was a Chiricahua Apache leader who resisted both Mexican and U.S. forces. After surrendering, he spent the rest of his life in U.S. captivity.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7d70-b026-b931bf88302b","description":"Geronimo","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-78d7-a31e-5a7b79c23bc7","description":"Poundmaker","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7e7c-9601-2ae563a7ad0d","description":"Sitting Bull","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7937-a962-3d0475834568","description":"Sequoyah","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-79be-b55c-9c43267325b7","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the first president to be impeached?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Senate acquitted Andrew Johnson, falling one vote short of the two-thirds majority needed to convict him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-704e-97cb-4d71c132bda6","description":"Andrew Johnson","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7183-8fb4-2e5114770f5e","description":"John Adams","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-71b2-bb80-68f83c19d26e","description":"Thomas Jefferson","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7d08-9d68-ba9b32df94b5","description":"James Madison","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7a2f-a397-57ec806b5e2c","category":"01a213