swer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7470-ab28-a54995052bee","description":"Battle of Trafalgar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-72f8-af94-792cdd2aa802","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which Israeli prime minister shared the 1978 Nobel Peace Prize with Anwar Sadat?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Menachem Begin and Anwar Sadat were honored for negotiating the Camp David Accords, which paved the way for a peace treaty between Egypt and Israel.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-79dc-a0f8-835d477d1ead","description":"Menachem Begin","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7850-859a-8cf4813f7896","description":"Golda Meir","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-73e1-8ff7-deef97ca017f","description":"Yitzhak Rabin","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f43-aca7-7abf25554277","description":"David Ben-Gurion","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7ee6-ad97-3fa18fca4fab","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which English king is traditionally said to have asked, \'Will no one rid me of this turbulent priest?\'","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Henry II\'s words are traditionally connected to Becket\'s murder by four knights in Canterbury Cathedral in 1170, though the exact wording is disputed.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7373-87b9-7b0719d61cb4","description":"Henry II","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-724b-9cce-7a6b70b0d099","description":"William I","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-761c-aeb7-eca50d237cd4","description":"Richard III","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7651-a0f8-dd8d46c019a3","description":"Henry VIII","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7370-8389-bc163b5ddafa","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"What was the primary language of the Aztecs?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Nahuatl is still spoken by Indigenous communities in Mexico today.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7ab7-8de3-0d344b3c3347","description":"Nahuatl","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7e60-a361-7f88780e526d","description":"Mayan","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7d86-80cb-8230a70fd3e1","description":"Mixtec","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-74c2-b97f-11b0903d360e","description":"Otomi","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-739e-a555-533d4cf71684","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the first king of Hungary?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"St. Stephen was canonized, and August 20, his feast day, is a national holiday in Hungary.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f63-8718-e34132970ac3","description":"St. Stephen","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7e95-93b5-78a1477acffd","description":"St. Marko","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7986-b1c7-cee5a424b82c","description":"St. Cyril","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7663-a91e-4526800a5128","description":"St. Alexander","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7b4a-a77d-f244cbd4b803","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"About how long did the American Civil War last?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The American Civil War lasted about four years, from 1861 to 1865. General Robert E. Lee\'s surrender at Appomattox in April 1865 marked a key turning point toward its end.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7429-a9fb-0e1f7836da5a","description":"Four years","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7c8b-91f5-2e8e30cdd959","description":"One year","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7c81-8837-4bd1203c1664","description":"Seven years","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f0f-a5a5-3737498678ef","description":"Ten years","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7852-ba9b-b60e8c58d749","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which battle was George A. Custer defeated?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"At the Battle of Little Bighorn, Lakota, Cheyenne, and