na Capac","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-77af-b4ab-fbe4f57dbdcd","description":"Pachacuti","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-760a-a6e3-d71a2c198ae5","description":"Tupac Amaru","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7cc9-a211-aa53caa8b58f","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which decade saw the Stonewall Riots in New York City, which helped to initiate the gay rights movement?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 1960s are correct: the Stonewall uprising began on June 28, 1969, after police raided the Stonewall Inn in Greenwich Village.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-754c-8036-2e0c3b11929a","description":"The 1960s","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f83-b512-4b77003dacae","description":"The 1950s","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7f85-8ca0-6120a2752cb8","description":"The 1970s","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-70e8-869b-f5ac8f15eb0f","description":"The 1980s","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7c66-815d-98d1101d0a1b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which of Henry VIII\'s six wives was fourth?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Anne of Cleves remained in England after the annulment and was treated as Henry VIII\u2019s \u201cbeloved sister.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad36-78c3-acbe-cb31286e0bed","description":"Anne of Cleves","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-77fb-b2b3-3071614fa66c","description":"Anne Boleyn","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7728-a5c0-3ad619ab89bf","description":"Catherine Parr","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-7375-8c6f-060edcbd3343","description":"Catherine of Aragon","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad36-72d7-8ae5-f220c3237903","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which law professor testified at Clarence Thomas\'s 1991 Supreme Court confirmation hearings?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Anita Hill\'s testimony accused Thomas of sexu