":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"When did the United States transfer the Panama Canal to Panamanian control?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The 1977 Torrijos\u2013Carter Treaties arranged a gradual transfer, with full Panamanian control taking effect on December 31, 1999.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7359-b4be-22a6de234e6a","description":"1999","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7f15-b673-c7b0d02f4311","description":"1987","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7564-badc-9968adb0c4db","description":"1991","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7530-af0c-54d1936ff001","description":"1979","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-705c-9ef6-99de6a495a80","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"How many children did Queen Victoria have?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Queen Victoria had nine children with Prince Albert. Their descendants married into royal families across Europe, helping earn Victoria her nickname.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-794b-923b-e782bebfaf1e","description":"Nine","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7f47-b14a-062237fff3a2","description":"Five","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-706a-9791-860103d2fbc7","description":"Seven","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-734a-9257-86dc0af30fb1","description":"Twelve","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7171-9083-bc0972463fdc","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the first European to sight New Zealand in 1642?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Abel Tasman was a Dutch explorer, and the sea between Australia and New Zealand is named after him.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-75cb-b418-8a390ac0dfd8","description":"Abel Tasman","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7afe-bd23-69d42082f979","description":"James Cook","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7a6e-9902-2d4ec91fd561","description":"Christopher Columbus","correct_answer":false},{"id":"