riefly known as the Batavian Republic?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Netherlands\' Batavian Republic was a French-backed successor to the Dutch Republic; in 1806, Napoleon replaced it with the Kingdom of Holland.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7e02-a667-e260c4917d69","description":"The Netherlands","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7cc4-8a63-2b7c802e353a","description":"Poland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-79b6-b566-94557b3f4b84","description":"Portugal","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7bca-8173-fbfabd9369c1","description":"Greece","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7764-8c61-7fe33dcea620","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Gulf War begin?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Gulf War began in 1990 after Iraq invaded Kuwait; the U.S.-led coalition launched Operation Desert Storm the following January.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7c88-a417-99d2b48498c0","description":"1990","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-79c6-af8c-c6493a4f211e","description":"1983","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-761e-a919-9c03ac50b9cd","description":"1971","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-78ae-8968-9aa6f7ca5d75","description":"1999","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-766b-9390-a3ab340f7218","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"The Battle of Rorke\'s Drift in 1879 featured in which war?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Zulu War was fought between the British Empire and the Zulu Kingdom. Rorke\'s Drift was one of its best-known engagements.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-78b6-b407-c1e5d58d0dd3","description":"Zulu War","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7328-8e1a-b4657ff040a8","description":"Vietnam War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7ad1-bd7d-addbde07f8a5","description":"Spanish Civil War","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-72b4-8e51-9f89e99ff899","description":"Russian Civil War","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-70d7-80b2-566f5e431d7e","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was born in Assisi in 1181 and later became a missionary?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"St. Francis founded the Order of Friars Minor, whose members are commonly called Franciscans.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-70cb-9cbe-8eaf370dd58b","description":"St. Francis","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-70dd-8f8c-252eacf29890","description":"St. Peter","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7a65-b4de-719ba256415e","description":"St. Paul","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7723-a477-ddb387eb403b","description":"St. Augustine","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7fb8-902d-3b7c0f22b61b","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In which year did the Boeing 747 enter regular passenger service?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The Boeing 747 entered regular passenger service in 1970, with Pan Am\'s inaugural commercial flight from New York to London.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-735e-99bd-76fb4d5af3c2","description":"1970","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-717b-b0a4-8cb37c33f862","description":"1966","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7383-9721-f0e80c76334f","description":"1974","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7a7c-9b5a-b0d26fe8d517","description":"1978","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-78be-9ce3-922c3f7fe39c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1956, Tunisia gained independence from which country?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Independence ended the French protectorate established in 1881; Habib Bourguiba became Tunisia\u2019s first president.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7d85-8072-dab8e0c75aff","description":"France","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7ae2-85b0-34a6b58b67d4","description":"Italy","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7e5d-8200-8f32ed3d23