ategory":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Which city was burned by General Sherman in 1864?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Atlanta was an important Confederate rail and supply center. Sherman\u2019s forces captured it in September 1864 and burned much of the city before beginning the March to the Sea.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7b2a-a538-73cd325fb1b5","description":"Atlanta","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7e53-8a84-72824da3bfb6","description":"Dallas","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7fd9-aa12-a71dc0f9c8eb","description":"Houston","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-70ee-90fd-7c0b070fe669","description":"Columbus","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-73c1-947b-48c36c897b33","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"Who was the 30th president of the USA, in term during the period 1923\u20131929?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Calvin Coolidge was nicknamed \u201cSilent Cal\u201d for his reserved manner and is associated with the phrase \u201cThe business of America is business.\u201d","alternatives":[{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7ada-ac33-2420f3df8ab6","description":"Calvin Coolidge","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7d13-a662-12acd631deab","description":"Martin Van Buren","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7d0c-abf0-543f7ce14c91","description":"Grover Cleveland","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-7a4f-b216-bb685c190292","description":"Rutherford B. Hayes","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a21904-ad37-756d-8e51-48cb69ca2a1c","category":"01a21312-b489-7ebc-94f2-41649ebfcaca","question":"In 1900, a sealed library cave holding tens of thousands of ancient manuscripts was found in which Buddhist cave complex in China\'s Gobi region?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The cache is often called the Dunhuang Library Cave. Its manuscripts include Buddhist scriptures as well as secular documents, and many are now held in institutions around the world.","alternatives"